interconnected dimensions (commonly physical, mental/emotional, social, and sometimes spiritual/cultural).","options":["An answer copied without understanding.","A guess with no reason.","Health has interconnected dimensions (commonly physical, mental/emotional, social, and sometimes spiritual/cultural).","A choice unrelated to safety, health or respect."],"question":"Which choice best shows accurate use of this idea about health dimensions?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nExample: Poor sleep (physical) → irritability (mental/emotional) → arguments with teammates (social). Strategy: earlier device cut-off supports more than one dimension.\n\nTRY FIRST\nGiven a short scenario, label two dimensions affected and propose one strategy that helps both.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: dimensions named accurately; strategy realistic and linked to both.","explain":"Health has interconnected dimensions (commonly physical, mental/emotional, social, and sometimes spiritual/cultural). A change in one dimension can affect others; strategies should notice the links.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make safe, healthy and respectful choices using clear cues and reasons, rather than guessing or copying others. Every choice keeps bodies safe and includes everyone.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the cues, rules or choices that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. For any movement, use a clear space, ask an adult to be nearby, move at your own comfortable level and stop if anything hurts or feels unsafe. You may always choose a gentler version or only describe the movement. One deliberate, reasoned change is more useful than a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Treating health as only sport fitness, or proposing unsafe “fixes.” Change the choice or strategy, not just the wording.","title":"Understand and demonstrate","visual":[{"alt":"Health dimensions.","caption":"Links m